## Battery (docs/development/perf-gate-baseline.md)
Quiet syscost boot (pa-boot 780s, syscost=1, KVM q35 smp2): census TERM 8 (6-10)/REFUSED 32 (28-36)/STRANDED no-1001ms-class, ticks >=99.5/s sustained, 0 panics/new OOM, syscall volume (load-gated window: load1<=9, foreign qemus<=8 — OTHER LANES RUN QEMUs; gate your enforcement window and prefer quiet windows), per-op avgs (clock_gettime 3-4us +-20%, nanosleep <=244ms). Then Tier-2 pbench fs-family cells (test/pbench_boot.py --bzimage <main bzImage>). Deliverable: refresh the Tier-1 table in docs/development/perf-gate-baseline.md (whole-table rule; provenance + load window per row) + written comparison vs the 2026-10-25 pa50main anchor. Out-of-band rows: rerun once in a quieter window before calling regression; root-cause regressions with data (the aarch64 merge's shared deltas are per-arch constants/failure-only prints).

## Discipline
One QEMU at a time (check ps before booting); 780s windows — queue doc edits between boots; kill only yours; pkill FORBIDDEN. bzImage = debug class, consistent with the anchor. Push to your branch (or a fresh one). Quota deaths: commit the partial table with provenance as you go.
Final message: lineage verdict (seed vs cooked), refreshed Tier-1 table w/ provenance, in/out-of-band verdicts + rerun evidence, commits.
